# Repository-wide generated-artifact backstop.
#
# Each module/project carries its own anchored .gitignore for the artifacts it
# produces.  Those patterns are deliberately anchored and module-specific so
# that committed teaching fixtures are never ignored.  This root file exists
# only to close the generic holes that are easy to miss when a new module is
# added: interpreter caches and host compiler droppings.
#
# Do NOT add broad data patterns here (e.g. *.dtb, *.dts, *.log, *.map,
# *.cpio.gz): several canonical modules intentionally commit small, bounded
# fixtures with exactly those extensions.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Host-side object files and linked host/target executables.  No module
# commits these; they are always reproducible from source.
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
*.img

# Editor / OS droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Pre-existing in-tree build output -----------------------------------------
# The Phase 1 Final Gate's own reviewer regression (`make test` in
# gates/phase-1-final) compiles reference fixtures in place and leaves the
# binaries and dependency files listed below untracked in that tree.  The
# Phase 2 Final Gate's check 13 asserts `git status gates/phase-1-final` is
# empty, so without these rules the canonical regression ORDER
# (Phase 1 `make test` then Phase 2 `make check`) fails spuriously.
# These paths are reproducible host build output and are never committed.
# Scoped by full path on purpose: a blanket `*.d` rule would be unsafe.
/gates/phase-1-final/part-b/variants/*/repro
/gates/phase-1-final/reviewer/part-a/reference/*.d
/gates/phase-1-final/reviewer/part-a/reference/sifter
/gates/phase-1-final/reviewer/part-a/reference/sifter_san
# Phase 1 `make test` also leaves object files and per-part build dirs behind.
/gates/phase-1-final/**/build/

# The Phase 2 Final Gate's `make check` builds all four parts in place and
# leaves firmware.elf/.asm/.map plus .d dependency files in part-*/build/.
# Same reasoning as above: reproducible build output, never committed, and the
# Phase 1 cleanliness assertion in that gate must not be tripped by its own
# sibling's build. Scoped by path so the tracked fixture trees that legitimately
# contain a directory named `build/` are untouched.
/gates/phase-2-final/*/build/
